---
import SiteLayout from "../../layouts/SiteLayout.astro";
import status from "../../data/status.json";
const osStatus = status.entries.find((entry) => entry.id === "aurora-os-public-evidence");
const browserStatus = status.entries.find((entry) => entry.id === "lumen-browser-public-evidence");
---
<SiteLayout title="Aurora — Independent computing. Built deliberately." description="Discover Aurora OS and Lumen, the Aurora Browser. Independent computing, built deliberately and documented with evidence.">
  <section class="reference-hero">
    <div class="shell reference-hero-inner">
      <div class="reference-hero-copy">
        <p class="eyebrow"><span class="eyebrow-line"></span> AN INDEPENDENT COMPUTING ECOSYSTEM</p>
        <h1>Build a better<br /><span>relationship with</span><br />your technology.</h1>
        <p class="reference-hero-description">Aurora is an independent project exploring a more deliberate approach to computing — from the foundations of an operating system to the tools people use every day.</p>
        <div class="hero-actions">
          <a class="button button-primary" href="#ecosystem">Explore the ecosystem <span aria-hidden="true">↘</span></a>
          <a class="text-link" href="https://github.com/Pokejoueur/aurora-website" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">View repository <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="reference-hero-art" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/aurora-hero.svg" alt="" width="760" height="480" fetchpriority="high" /></div>
      <div class="reference-hero-index"><span>01 / 02 <i></i></span><span>ONE ECOSYSTEM · MULTIPLE WORKSTREAMS</span></div>
    </div>
  </section>
  <section class="reference-principles" aria-label="Aurora principles"><div class="shell reference-principles-inner"><span>SECURITY BY DESIGN</span><b aria-hidden="true">✦</b><span>OPEN ENGINEERING</span><b aria-hidden="true">✦</b><span>MEASURED PROGRESS</span><b aria-hidden="true">✦</b><span>USER SOVEREIGNTY</span></div></section>
  <section class="audience-start shell" aria-labelledby="audience-start-title">
    <div class="audience-start-heading">
      <p class="eyebrow"><span class="eyebrow-line"></span> YOUR NEXT STEP</p>
      <h2 id="audience-start-title">What brings you to Aurora?</h2>
      <p>Whether you want to understand the products or work on the code, start with the path that fits you.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="audience-start-grid">
      <a href="/en/docs/getting-started/" class="audience-start-card">
        <span>01 / EXPLORING AURORA</span>
        <strong>I'm here to learn or use Aurora.</strong>
        <small>Explore Aurora OS and Lumen, check current availability and find user-facing guidance.</small>
        <b>START HERE <i aria-hidden="true">↗</i></b>
      </a>
      <a href="/en/docs/developer-guide/" class="audience-start-card">
        <span>02 / BUILDING AURORA</span>
        <strong>I'm here to develop or contribute.</strong>
        <small>Set up the website repository, understand the architecture and follow the contribution workflow.</small>
        <b>OPEN DEVELOPER GUIDE <i aria-hidden="true">↗</i></b>
      </a>
    </div>
  </section>
  <section class="home-principles shell" id="principles">
    <div class="home-principles-heading"><p class="eyebrow"><span class="eyebrow-line"></span> PRINCIPLES</p><h2>Technology should<br /><span>work for people.</span></h2></div>
    <div class="home-principles-grid">
      <article><span>01 / PRIVACY</span><h3>Privacy by default.</h3><p>Minimize unnecessary data collection and make data handling understandable and controllable.</p></article>
      <article><span>02 / SECURITY</span><h3>Security by design.</h3><p>Treat privilege boundaries and failure containment as architectural responsibilities.</p></article>
      <article><span>03 / CLARITY</span><h3>Understandable systems.</h3><p>Prefer inspectable decisions, maintainable components and clear technical documentation.</p></article>
      <article><span>04 / SOVEREIGNTY</span><h3>User sovereignty.</h3><p>Give users meaningful control over their computing environment and its behavior.</p></article>
    </div>
  </section>
  <section class="reference-ecosystem shell" id="ecosystem">
    <div class="reference-ecosystem-intro"><p class="eyebrow"><span class="eyebrow-line"></span> THE ECOSYSTEM</p><h2>Two products.<br /><span>One direction.</span></h2><p>Aurora OS and Lumen are the products. This platform connects them through documentation, add-ons, extensions and verifiable project updates.</p></div>
    <div class="reference-project-grid">
      <a class="reference-project-card" href="/en/ecosystem/os/"><div class="reference-card-top"><span>01</span><span class="reference-status"><i></i> {osStatus?.reportedProgress ?? 70}% REPORTED</span></div><div><p class="project-type">OPERATING SYSTEM</p><h3>Aurora OS</h3><p>A from-scratch operating system in Rust, designed around a capability-based microkernel. The project reports an estimated {osStatus?.reportedProgress ?? 70}% development progress.</p></div><span class="reference-card-link">EXPLORE AURORA OS ↗</span></a>
      <a class="reference-project-card" href="/en/ecosystem/browser/"><div class="reference-card-top"><span>02</span><span class="reference-status"><i></i> {browserStatus?.reportedStage?.toUpperCase() ?? "IN DEVELOPMENT"}</span></div><div><p class="project-type">WEB BROWSER</p><h3>Lumen <small>/ Aurora Browser</small></h3><p>The Aurora Browser is in development. Its architecture, compatibility and security properties will be documented as they are implemented and verified.</p></div><span class="reference-card-link">EXPLORE LUMEN ↗</span></a>
    </div>
  </section>
  <section class="reference-approach" id="approach"><div class="shell reference-approach-inner"><div class="reference-approach-heading"><p class="eyebrow"><span class="eyebrow-line"></span> THE APPROACH</p><h2>Ambition is easy.<br /><span>Engineering is proof.</span></h2></div><p class="reference-approach-lead">We believe the foundations of computing deserve the same care as the experiences built on top of them.</p><div class="reference-approach-point"><span>01</span><p>Understandable<br />by design</p></div><div class="reference-approach-point"><span>02</span><p>Security is<br />structural</p></div><div class="reference-approach-point"><span>03</span><p>Evidence over<br />claims</p></div></div></section>
  <section class="home-section shell" id="engineering"><div class="home-section-heading"><div><p class="eyebrow"><span class="eyebrow-line"></span> ENGINEERING</p><h2>Built from the<br /><span>foundations.</span></h2></div><p>Engineering pages explain the architecture, trust boundaries and trade-offs behind Aurora. Product implementation claims remain separate from architectural intent.</p></div><div class="home-link-grid"><a href="/en/engineering/architecture/"><span>01 / ARCHITECTURE</span><strong>System architecture</strong><small>Responsibilities, boundaries and interfaces ↗</small></a><a href="/en/engineering/security/"><span>02 / SECURITY</span><strong>Security model</strong><small>Threats, privileges and limitations ↗</small></a><a href="/en/engineering/privacy/"><span>03 / PRIVACY</span><strong>Privacy approach</strong><small>Data handling and policy status ↗</small></a></div></section>
  <section class="home-section home-section-alt" id="development"><div class="shell"><div class="home-section-heading"><div><p class="eyebrow"><span class="eyebrow-line"></span> DEVELOPMENT</p><h2>Progress you can<br /><span>inspect.</span></h2></div><p>Product stages are reported transparently. The OS percentage is a project estimate; it is not a substitute for subsystem-level implementation and test evidence.</p></div><div class="home-status-panel"><div><span class="home-status-number">01</span><strong>Aurora OS</strong><span class="status-label">{osStatus?.reportedProgress ?? 70}% REPORTED</span><p>Project-reported development estimate. This is not a verified readiness score or a claim that an installable, production-ready OS exists.</p></div><div><span class="home-status-number">02</span><strong>Lumen Browser</strong><span class="status-label">{browserStatus?.reportedStage?.toUpperCase() ?? "IN DEVELOPMENT"}</span><p>Lumen is being developed. Browser capabilities, compatibility and security properties are not presented as verified.</p></div></div><a class="text-link" href="/en/development/">Explore development status and roadmap ↗</a></div></section>
  <section class="home-section shell" id="documentation"><div class="home-section-heading"><div><p class="eyebrow"><span class="eyebrow-line"></span> DOCUMENTATION</p><h2>Understand how<br /><span>Aurora works.</span></h2></div><p>Documentation is organized around exploring the ecosystem, using products when releases exist, and understanding how to develop them.</p></div><div class="home-link-grid"><a href="/en/docs/getting-started/"><span>01 / ORIENTATION</span><strong>Getting started</strong><small>Understand the projects and their current status ↗</small></a><a href="/en/docs/user-guide/"><span>02 / USERS</span><strong>User documentation</strong><small>Installation and usage guides when available ↗</small></a><a href="/en/docs/developer-guide/"><span>03 / DEVELOPERS</span><strong>Developer documentation</strong><small>Architecture, setup and contribution ↗</small></a></div></section>
  <section class="home-section home-community"><div class="shell home-community-inner"><div><p class="eyebrow"><span class="eyebrow-line"></span> COMMUNITY</p><h2>Built openly.<br /><span>Improved together.</span></h2><p>Start with the public website repository. Additional community channels will be listed once configured and verified.</p></div><a class="button button-primary" href="/en/community/">Community and contributions <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a></div></section>
</SiteLayout>
